  "question": {
    "text": "The acceleration due to gravity on the surface of earth is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi></math>. If the diameter of earth reduces to half of its original value and mass remains constant, then acceleration due to gravity on the surface of earth would be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "D"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The acceleration due to gravity is related to the mass and the radius of the Earth by the formula:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>g</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">G</mi><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">M</mi></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">⇒</mo><mi>g</mi><mo mathvariant=\"italic\">∝</mo><mfrac><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">1</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"italic\">R</mi><mn mathvariant=\"italic\">2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo> </mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mn>1</mn></mfenced></math></p><p>Thus, from equation (1), it follows that</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo> </mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mfrac><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><msup><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><msub><mi>R</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>g</mi></math></p>"
  }
}